                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A crying shame this had to crash and burn the way it did and leave an unfinished cliffhanger ending but it's worth a brief playthrough if you can pick this up on sale or in a bundle. There's some jankiness but it's forgiveable. It definitely could've used a little more polish but it's enjoyable. Beautiful setting if you like Victorian-inspired fantasy steampunk settings. Also has a strong feeling of having been inspired by the American McGee Alice games and some fans from there may enjoy this.\n\nIf this dev ever returns to gaming I'd eagerly be interesting to see what else they could concoct. I love this style of imagination, even if it's a super-short romp and not a highly complex or involved game.",
